This is an independent Linux-first program. The game message formats it reads were
worked out by others, and its code was written with their work as reference:

  - Pet Tracker by 0Fox2Give (https://github.com/0Fox2Give/PetTracker), GPL-3.0-only:
    framing and identity message layouts.
  - A2Tools-DPS-Meter by taengu (https://github.com/taengu/A2Tools-DPS-Meter), GPL-3.0:
    the skill hit, player name and class layouts, the class colours and the KDE
    window-rule approach for overlays above fullscreen games (no code copied).

The capture, framing and decoding code is shared with Arno's Pet Tracker.

The GPL grant covers this project's code. It does not cover game names or other game
